WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.370
"Golden vs Brown Flaxseed:
Which Has More Benefits?"

00:00:06.812 --> 00:00:10.000
Embellished as a so-called
miraculous defense

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.040
against some critical maladies,

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:14.720
flaxseeds are one
of the original health foods,

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:17.600
going back thousands of years
to the time of Hippocrates.

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:20.040
You can buy them in bulk
for about three bucks a pound,

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:21.800
which would last you
nearly two months

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:24.220
at the one-tablespoon-a-day dose
I recommend

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:27.280
in my Dr. Greger's
Daily Dozen app.

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:30.320
Flaxseeds come with
nature's own finest packaging:

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:32.960
a hard natural hull
that keeps them fresh inside.

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:34.640
Unfortunately,
nature's packaging

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:35.840
is a little too good.

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:37.280
If we eat flaxseeds whole,

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:39.120
they are likely to just pass
right through us,

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:41.880
come out the other end,
and not do us much good.

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:43.840
So, chew them really well,

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:45.880
or grind them
in a coffee or spice grinder,

00:00:45.880 --> 00:00:47.960
a mini food processor,
a good blender,

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:50.320
or just buy them
already ground.

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:52.960
Ground flaxseeds can be stored
for months at room temperature

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:55.640
in an airtight container.

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:57.680
Ground flaxseeds have
a nice binding quality

00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:01.280
that makes for thick, rich
milkshake-y-type smoothies.

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:03.160
In fact, you can use
ground flaxseeds

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:04.840
to replace eggs in baking.

00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:06.560
For each egg in a recipe,

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:08.320
blend one tablespoon
of ground flax

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:09.600
with three tablespoons of water

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:11.560
until it gets all gooey.

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:14.960
With that swap, you'd be
actively lowering cholesterol--

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:17.880
based on more than five dozen
randomized controlled trials--

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:21.760
rather than raising it
as the eggs would've.

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:25.680
There are brown flaxseeds
and golden flaxseeds.

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:28.400
Brown ones may have
about 20 percent more omega-3s

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:29.080
than golden,

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:32.800
but, like, 30% more
antioxidant power.

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:35.400
They both lower blood pressures
similarly,

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:37.040
but golden flax appears better

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:39.000
at lowering cholesterol levels.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:41.880
Both golden and brown
helped seal a leaky gut,

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:46.040
but brown seems better
at reducing endotoxemia.

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:48.600
Far as I'm concerned,
brown wins,

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:50.960
because brown flaxseed
beats out golden

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:53.120
with 60 percent more lignans,

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:57.160
those anticancer compounds
activated by our gut flora.

00:01:57.160 --> 00:01:59.520
That's the main reason
ground flax is better

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:03.360
than flaxseed oil, in addition
to being more stable.

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:04.800
Ground flaxseeds don't oxidize

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:06.840
even after nearly a year
at room temperature

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:08.400
in an airtight container,

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:11.120
presumably because they are
packed with antioxidants.

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:13.720
But strip those away
to make flaxseed oil,

00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:17.200
and it can start to turn rancid
within a matter of weeks.

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:21.160
The lignans are also
stripped away in flax oil.

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:22.320
If you look at the ingredients

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:26.600
of so-called "high lignan"
flaxseed oils, it's a scam.

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:29.440
They just sprinkle in
some ground flax into the oil

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:31.560
to add a pittance.

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:34.120
Lignans are why flaxseeds
are so powerful

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:36.320
at dampening
the effects of estrogen.

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:39.160
Eating just a single tablespoon
of ground flaxseeds a day

00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:42.200
extends the length
of a woman's menstrual cycle--

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:43.520
not the menses itself,

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:45.240
but the whole month-long cycle--

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:47.760
by an average of about one day.

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:49.560
Beyond improving ovulation

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:51.640
and reducing
common PMS symptoms

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:53.520
such as breast pain
and cramping,

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:55.560
the lengthening of the cycle

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:58.040
means you have fewer periods
throughout your life,

00:02:58.040 --> 00:02:59.880
which means
less estrogen exposure

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:03.320
and lower breast cancer risk.

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:05.680
Lignans may explain
why flaxseed consumption

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:08.320
is associated with a lower risk
of getting breast cancer

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:09.840
and dying from it,

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:11.880
whereas greater antibiotic use

00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:13.440
is associated
with an increased risk

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:15.320
of getting and dying
from breast cancer,

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:17.480
presumably because antibiotics
can wipe out

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:19.240
some of the good bacteria
in our colon

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:21.920
that activate
the anticancer activity

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:24.880
of flaxseed lignans.

00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:26.400
Check out my videos
on preventing

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:30.080
and treating breast cancer
with flax.

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:32.320
Flax is good for men, too,

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:34.400
improving enlarged
prostate symptoms

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:37.000
comparable to common drugs
that are used,

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:39.720
that can cause a wide array
of adverse side effects

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:41.000
including impotence,

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:42.680
whereas the side effects
of flax

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:44.080
are not only lower cholesterol,

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:46.560
but better blood pressures,
better blood sugars,

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:49.200
and maybe fewer hot flashes,

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:51.000
though that's not
usually a big problem

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:54.909
in sufferers
of enlarged prostates.

